WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.760
What helps set the front edges of the Hox code?

2
00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:08.160
A signal made from vitamin A.

3
00:00:09.133 --> 00:00:13.873
Retinoic acid is made from retinol, which is vitamin A, in two steps.

4
00:00:14.873 --> 00:00:19.853
Raldh2, the main enzyme for the last step, is made in mesoderm beside the posterior

5
00:00:19.853 --> 00:00:21.553
hindbrain and spinal cord.

6
00:00:22.567 --> 00:00:24.967
Cyp26 enzymes destroy it.

7
00:00:25.707 --> 00:00:28.887
Cyp26a1 is strong toward the front of the neural plate.

8
00:00:29.867 --> 00:00:33.187
Picture a bath, with the tap at the back and the drain at the front.

9
00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:37.287
Retinoic acid ends up high at the back and low at the front.

10
00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:42.350
In the nucleus, it binds the retinoic acid receptor, RAR.

11
00:00:43.190 --> 00:00:49.110
RAR pairs with its partner, RXR, on short DNA sequences called response elements.

12
00:00:50.183 --> 00:00:53.043
Hoxa1 and Hoxb1 carry these elements.

13
00:00:53.963 --> 00:00:58.983
In cell culture, 3′ Hox genes respond to lower doses than 5′ genes.

14
00:01:00.117 --> 00:01:05.117
In a simple threshold model, then, fewer Hox genes come on toward the front, where

15
00:01:05.117 --> 00:01:06.117
the signal is lower.

16
00:01:07.117 --> 00:01:12.517
Predict. Give mouse embryos extra retinoic acid at an early stage.

17
00:01:13.377 --> 00:01:14.937
Which way should the Hox edges move?

18
00:01:21.350 --> 00:01:28.190
Forward. In 1992, Marshall, Krumlauf, Lumsden and colleagues found the hindbrain Hox

19
00:01:28.290 --> 00:01:29.290
domains changed.

20
00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:34.180
Rhombomeres two and three shifted toward the identity of four and five.

21
00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:37.840
Too much signal shows a response, not the normal role.

22
00:01:38.833 --> 00:01:41.533
Predict. Now block the drain.

23
00:01:42.573 --> 00:01:46.593
Mice lacking Cyp26a1 clear less retinoic acid at the front.

24
00:01:47.493 --> 00:01:48.493
What changes?

25
00:01:54.617 --> 00:01:59.497
The front shifts: the front of the hindbrain looked partly transformed toward a more

26
00:01:59.497 --> 00:02:00.557
posterior character.

27
00:02:01.650 --> 00:02:06.870
Remove the tap instead, in mice lacking Raldh2, and the posterior hindbrain is

28
00:02:06.870 --> 00:02:07.870
poorly patterned.

29
00:02:12.050 --> 00:02:15.510
Changing the signal sets the direction, not the exact edges.

30
00:02:16.533 --> 00:02:20.593
In the hindbrain, group 2 genes reach farther forward than group 1.

31
00:02:21.033 --> 00:02:23.333
Yet 3′ prime genes need less signal.

32
00:02:24.173 --> 00:02:25.973
So other inputs help set those edges.

33
00:02:27.017 --> 00:02:30.517
Retinoids are teratogens, agents that cause birth defects.

34
00:02:31.457 --> 00:02:35.397
In mouse and chick, extra retinoic acid early shifts the Hox code.

35
00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:40.160
It also disturbs the neural crest cells that build much of the face.

36
00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:44.400
In humans, this mechanism is inferred from animal work.

37
00:02:48.733 --> 00:02:53.693
More early retinoic acid gives a more posterior code; the code helps set the

38
00:02:53.693 --> 00:02:56.973
neurons. Other inputs help draw the final edges.
